        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-08T12:51:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It took me a couple of games to see KNYFE go crazy. Now that I have, I have a reasonably good handle on how do treat this Complexity One hero. Was it obvious to everyone else that she’s like a console fighter game&nbsp; character?</p><p>Here’s what I mean. (I’m omitting draws for clarity) During my mostly weekly game night, we were playing Vengeance, and I had Focusing Conduit-Blade and Battlefield Experience out. I played For the Greater Good, which played “Energy Burn” for 7 and used Battlefield Experience’s power. Net 13 to Baron Blade. This destroyed BE so I drew a card and played Amplified Combatant to get to 17 to the Baron. That was the play phase. Then I used my regular power to net 20 to the Baron and drew a card.</p><p>While this will almost never come to pass – too many cards lined up nicely – I can see how it could go on through most of the deck. I felt like I was hitting “Punch punch kick, punch punch kick…”</p><p>Does this line up with everyone else's experience with the character?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:43.783Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
